{"parentUuid":"4002cae4-6f62-4438-86d7-d209096ebfa4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a944a82f6940ae23a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Zip3cfX6Tw6kQ9pKQooPz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" pull request emscripten WebAssembly 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[Help] Compiling OR-Tools to WebAssembly with Emscripten\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/ESK9oknRrK8\"},{\"title\":\"Building to WebAssembly — Emscripten 5.0.8-git (dev) documentation\",\"url\":\"https://emscripten.org/docs/compiling/WebAssembly.html\"},{\"title\":\"WebAssembly - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebAssembly\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - emscripten-core/emscripten: Emscripten: An LLVM-to-WebAssembly Compiler · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: A browser-friendly version of or-tools (emscripten) · Issue #1670 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1670\"},{\"title\":\"Main — Emscripten 5.0.8-git (dev) documentation\",\"url\":\"https://emscripten.org/\"},{\"title\":\"About Emscripten — Emscripten 5.0.8-git (dev) documentation\",\"url\":\"https://emscripten.org/docs/introducing_emscripten/about_emscripten.html\"},{\"title\":\"Port it to the web with Web assembly and Emscripten - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/baduit/port-it-to-the-web-with-web-assembly-and-emscripten-5c7k\"},{\"title\":\"Emscripten download | SourceForge.net\",\"url\":\"https://sourceforge.net/projects/emscripten.mirror/\"},{\"title\":\"Emscripten Compiler Frontend (emcc) — Emscripten 5.0.8-git (dev) documentation\",\"url\":\"https://emscripten.org/docs/tools_reference/emcc.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding OR-Tools pull requests related to Emscripten and WebAssembly in 2025:\n\n## Recent OR-Tools Emscripten Work\n\nOR-Tools is currently testing an experimental Emscripten build with a GitHub workflow at amd64_web.yml, including a Dockerfile for web setup, though tests have been disabled since EXPECT_DEATH is not available.\n\n## Historical Context\n\nThere was experimental work on OR-Tools WebAssembly compilation almost five years ago, including Pull Request #2404 for adding Wasm32 as a cross-compilation target.\n\nEmscripten support is currently a low priority with zero human resources allocated to it, but the project would be receptive to contributions with nice usage samples.\n\nThe search results indicate that while OR-Tools has experimental WebAssembly/Emscripten support in development, there doesn't appear to be specific information about a particular 2025 pull request in these results. For more detailed information about specific pull requests, you may want to check the Google OR-Tools GitHub repository directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"327bba0c-2408-4f74-890b-8d85689d55bb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:06.171Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4002cae4-6f62-4438-86d7-d209096ebfa4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0b288a61-b39c-4e51-a0fd-e41c031671c8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a944a82f6940ae23a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C7CmNiHWA6o5GqGp4cTHJY","type":"tool_result","content":"# OR-Tools WebAssembly Compilation Status\n\nBased on the provided GitHub issue, I cannot provide information about the current status of OR-Tools WebAssembly compilation, progress made in 2024-2026, available solvers in the Emscripten build, or performance benchmarks.\n\nThe webpage content shows only **Issue #4443**, which is a feature request opened on November 18, 2024. The user asks: \"I am interested in running constraint problems from the browser either with the C++ or Python interface. I would like to know if something like this is possible.\"\n\nThis appears to be an **open inquiry rather than an announcement of available functionality**. The issue was assigned to a team member (Mizux) and tagged with \"Feature Request\" and \"Lang: WASM\" labels, but the content provided contains no technical details about implementation status, solver availability, or performance data.\n\nTo obtain current information about WebAssembly support for OR-Tools, you would need to check the project's official documentation, recent pull requests, or release notes beyond what appears in this issue."}]},"uuid":"8218edcc-45d7-4895-ab58-6aeb716ef5f9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:07.221Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0b288a61-b39c-4e51-a0fd-e41c031671c8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"13f72753-fad1-41e3-918b-869fa1801909","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a944a82f6940ae23a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C5F6L5ZkYNmS2yGYJKauL8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"WebGPU compute solver optimization 2025 LP MIP\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GPU-Accelerated Optimization with GAMS and NVIDIA cuOpt\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/blog/2025/09/gpu-accelerated-optimization-with-gams-and-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - NVIDIA/cuopt: GPU accelerated decision optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuopt\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerate Decision Optimization Using Open Source NVIDIA cuOpt | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/accelerate-decision-optimization-using-open-source-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"GPU-Accelerated Primal Heuristics for Mixed Integer Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.20499v1\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerate Large Linear Programming Problems with NVIDIA cuOpt | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/accelerate-large-linear-programming-problems-with-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"First-order methods in Linear Programming: PDHG and GPU-friendly LP solvers | Ebrahim Pichka\",\"url\":\"https://epichka.com/blog/2026/fom-lp/\"},{\"title\":\"The Year 2025 for GAMS Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/blog/2026/01/the-year-2025-for-gams-solvers/\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS and NVIDIA cuOpt: Driving open-source innovation in optimization – School of Mathematics\",\"url\":\"https://blogs.ed.ac.uk/mathematics/2025/03/18/highs-and-nvidia-cuopt-driving-open-source-innovation-in-optimization/\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS - High-performance parallel linear optimization software\",\"url\":\"https://highs.dev/\"},{\"title\":\"cuOpt | Decision Optimization | NVIDIA\",\"url\":\"https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai-data-science/products/cuopt/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding WebGPU compute solver optimization for LP and MIP in 2025:\n\n## GPU-Accelerated Optimization Trends in 2025\n\nA major trend in 2025 was the adoption of Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient (PDHG) algorithms, which are first-order methods designed for extremely large-scale linear programs (LP) where traditional methods may struggle and requirements on feasibility and optimality may be lower.\n\n## Key GPU-Accelerated Solvers\n\nNVIDIA cuOpt is a GPU-accelerated optimization engine that excels in mixed integer linear programming (MILP), linear programming (LP), quadratic programming (QP), and vehicle routing problems (VRP). cuOpt solves LP, MIP, and VRP problems 10x to 5,000x faster with GPU acceleration and is available as open source under the Apache 2.0 license.\n\n## Performance Improvements\n\nThe NVIDIA cuOpt LP solver achieves over 5,000x faster performance compared to CPU-based solvers by leveraging the Primal-Dual Linear Programming (PDLP) algorithm and NVIDIA GPU acceleration, which is a first-order method that uses the derivative of the problem to iteratively optimize the objective and minimize constraint violation.\n\n## Integration with Existing Solvers\n\nThe cuOpt heuristic mixed-integer programming (MIP) solver, when paired with HiGHS, enhances performance beyond what either solver can achieve alone—when running MIPLIB benchmarks with a 5-minute time limit, HiGHS alone achieves results with a 28% gap from optimality, but when integrated with cuOpt running on a H100 GPU, the gap from optimality improves to 21%.\n\nNote: The search results focus on NVIDIA cuOpt and GPU acceleration rather than WebGPU specifically, which represents the practical direction of GPU-accelerated optimization in 2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7ef4d873-984b-467e-8f74-b7be78d6529b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:08.529Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"13f72753-fad1-41e3-918b-869fa1801909","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
