{"parentUuid":"bd55b135-3da7-4ba2-8913-936e727b4827","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a944a82f6940ae23a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019YeDMtSfrZrXGHffMsZr83","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"WebAssembly\" \"168 hour\" OR \"long running\" compute solver feasibility\"\n\nNo links found.\n\nI've performed the web search for your query about WebAssembly, 168-hour or long-running compute solvers, and feasibility. However, the search didn't return any results. This suggests that there may not be widely available public information on this specific combination of topics online, or the exact phrasing might need to be adjusted.\n\nIf you're researching this topic, you might try:\n- Searching for more general terms like \"WebAssembly long-running computations\"\n- Looking for specific solver implementations (e.g., optimization solvers, constraint solvers)\n- Checking academic papers or technical documentation from WebAssembly development resources\n- Searching without the \"168 hour\" timeframe specification\n\nWould you like me to try a different search query with modified terms?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d6abd3aa-dd26-4638-9aa6-378d6dc1dca9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:17.142Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bd55b135-3da7-4ba2-8913-936e727b4827","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ae7020bd-1695-4b50-9869-7b961559c138","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a944a82f6940ae23a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EsaPAQzM9RPKKDbALgiTZT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT performance overhead native vs WASM benchmark constraint programming\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"> “Near-Native Performance”: Wasm is often described as having “near-native perf... | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=30156437\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"},{\"title\":\"C++ VS Wasm benchmarks, Which programming language or compiler is faster\",\"url\":\"https://programming-language-benchmarks.vercel.app/cpp-vs-wasm\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - zandaqo/iswasmfast: Performance comparison of WebAssembly, C++ Addon, and native implementations of various algorithms in Node.js.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/zandaqo/iswasmfast\"},{\"title\":\"The WebAssembly value proposition is write once, not performance | nickb.dev\",\"url\":\"https://nickb.dev/blog/the-webassembly-value-proposition-is-write-once-not-performance/\"},{\"title\":\"Analyzing the Performance of WebAssembly vs. Native Code\",\"url\":\"https://www.usenix.org/system/files/atc19-jangda.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Performance drops from 60s to 700s - why? · Issue #1102 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1102\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about WebAssembly (WASM) vs native performance overhead in general, though the results don't contain specific benchmarks comparing CP-SAT native vs WASM implementations.\n\n## General WASM vs Native Performance\n\nThe search results indicate that WebAssembly performance overhead compared to native code varies:\n\nBROWSIX-WASM imposes very low overhead, averaging only 0.2% with a maximum of 1.2% on SPEC benchmarks. However, other benchmarks show different results. In a hashing microbenchmark using Wasm SIMD, Wasm was 4x slower than native at large payloads, partly due to Wasm SIMD being limited to 128 bit registers compared to the 256 bit AVX2 implementation.\n\nThe Sharp Wasm benchmarks show that sometimes Wasm can be very competitive with native implementations, and sometimes it is not.\n\n## CP-SAT Information\n\nWhile the search results contain general information about the CP-SAT Solver combining constraint programming (CP) techniques with Boolean satisfiability (SAT) solving technology, there are no specific benchmarks comparing CP-SAT native versus WASM performance overhead in the results. To find this specific information, you would likely need to check the official Google OR-Tools documentation or GitHub repository for performance comparisons, as they may have published detailed benchmarks for different deployment targets.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0e6bbcf0-9b75-40e2-a638-c5a4c989d219","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:20.776Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ae7020bd-1695-4b50-9869-7b961559c138","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"174852f8-2a02-4afb-b41b-d7abf3c51975","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a944a82f6940ae23a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019kftSHxuxn5Ndt73JuMAB9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"WebAssembly Component Model SAT solver 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"WebAssembly: The High-Performance Web in 2026\",\"url\":\"https://blog.weskill.org/2026/04/webassembly-high-performance-web-in-2026.html\"},{\"title\":\"WebAssembly in 2026: Where It Has Landed, What WASI 0.2 Changes, and Why Java and Kotlin Developers Should Pay Attention Now - Java Code Geeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.javacodegeeks.com/2026/04/webassembly-in-2026-where-it-has-landed-what-wasi-0-2-changes-and-why-java-and-kotlin-developers-should-pay-attention-now.html\"},{\"title\":\"WebAssembly in 2026: Three Years of \\\"Almost Ready\\\" - Java Code Geeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.javacodegeeks.com/2026/04/webassembly-in-2026-three-years-of-almost-ready.html\"},{\"title\":\"The State of WebAssembly – 2025 and 2026\",\"url\":\"https://platform.uno/blog/the-state-of-webassembly-2025-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The WebAssembly Component Model\",\"url\":\"https://component-model.bytecodealliance.org/\"},{\"title\":\"WASI and the WebAssembly Component Model: Current Status - eunomia\",\"url\":\"https://eunomia.dev/blog/2025/02/16/wasi-and-the-webassembly-component-model-current-status/\"},{\"title\":\"WebAssembly Component Model: The 2026 Developer Cheat Sheet\",\"url\":\"https://techbytes.app/posts/wasm-component-model-cheat-sheet/\"},{\"title\":\"The WebAssembly Component Model (WAW 2025 - - WebAssembly Workshop) - POPL 2025\",\"url\":\"https://popl25.sigplan.org/details/waw-2025-papers/4/The-WebAssembly-Component-Model\"},{\"title\":\"WebAssembly Component Model: Wasm in 2026 — Cristhian Villegas\",\"url\":\"https://blog.iamcristhian.dev/2026/04/webassembly-component-model-wasm-beyond-browser-2026\"},{\"title\":\"WASI 1.0: You Won't Know When WebAssembly Is Everywhere in 2026 - The New Stack\",\"url\":\"https://thenewstack.io/wasi-1-0-you-wont-know-when-webassembly-is-everywhere-in-2026/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found extensive information about WebAssembly Component Model in 2026, but there is **no information about SAT solvers** in relation to WebAssembly or the Component Model in the search results.\n\nHere's what the search revealed about the WebAssembly Component Model in 2026:\n\n## WebAssembly Component Model in 2026\n\nThe most significant shift in 2026 is the Wasm Component Model, which uses WIT (WebAssembly Interface Type) to allow developers to treat Wasm modules like standard JavaScript libraries.\n\nThe WebAssembly Component Model is one of the most interesting ideas in the ecosystem, solving the core problem that WebAssembly's type system is deliberately minimal by using WIT (WebAssembly Interface Types) to give components a shared contract language.\n\nWASI 0.2 introduced the Component Model and a proper interface type system. The Component Model is being adjusted with native async support and the WASI worlds are being modified to take advantage of the new async capabilities, with this work expected to be complete in February 2026 and released as WASI 0.3.\n\nHowever, regarding SAT solvers specifically: the search results do not contain any information about SAT solver integration, development, or use cases with WebAssembly or the Component Model in 2026. If you're looking for specific information about SAT solvers and WebAssembly, you may want to search for more specialized resources on that topic.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fb800311-1211-4a87-b386-3c59d7a296b6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:20.793Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"174852f8-2a02-4afb-b41b-d7abf3c51975","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fb800311-1211-4a87-b386-3c59d7a296b6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a944a82f6940ae23a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013xkhHAqxH5PVHgDwL8JRLc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough information. Let me synthesize the findings.\n\n# WASM 跑 SAT/CP 求解器调研（2024-2026）\n\n## 1. OR-Tools WASM 状态：边缘探索，非生产\n\n- Google OR-Tools 有**实验性** Emscripten build（GitHub workflow `amd64_web.yml` + Docker 配置），但官方说法：\"Emscripten 当前低优先级，零人力投入\"\n- Issue #4443（2024-11）和 #1670（更早）都还是 feature request 状态\n- 关键限制：WASM build 下**只有 CP-SAT 和 GLOP**可用，第三方求解器（Gurobi/CBC/SCIP）全部禁用\n- WASM 测试默认禁用，因为 `EXPECT_DEATH` 在 WASM 下不可用——意味着没有正式 CI 覆盖\n- **结论：OR-Tools 没有官方 WASM 支持，自己编译能跑但是踩坑路径**\n\n## 2. SAT solver WASM 移植情况\n\n- **MiniSat**：成熟（jgalenson 的 demo 跑了多年），但 MiniSat 性能远落后于现代 SAT solver\n- **Z3 SMT**：`z3-solver` npm 包（v4.16.0，2025-2026）已是相对成熟方案；TypeScript bindings 完整；性能\"native 的 1/2 到 1/5\"（cpitclaudel/z3.wasm）；冷启动 Chrome ~15s / Firefox <1s\n- **CaDiCaL/Kissat WASM 移植：搜不到任何官方/社区维护的端口**。SAT Competition 2025 提交也没有 WASM 版本。Kissat 是裸金属 C 代码，理论可编 emscripten，但没人做\n\n## 3. WASI 标准 2024-2026\n\n- WASI 0.2（2024）：Component Model 落地，async I/O 进入预览\n- WASI 0.3（2026-02 发布）：原生 async/await，但**线程支持仍是 gap**\n- WASI 1.0 生产稳定：目标 2026 年底 / 2027 初\n- 多线程标准化没进 0.3 路线图，CP-SAT 这种重度多线程求解器**短期内无法走 WASI 标准路径**多核\n\n## 4. 性能数字（关键）\n\n- Chrome/Firefox WASM 对 CPU 密集任务：**95%+ native 性能**（Rust+Wasm 报告 8-10x 比 JS 快）\n- WASM SIMD 128-bit 全主流浏览器支持，但仍弱于 native AVX2/AVX-512（hashing 测试 WASM SIMD 比 native 慢 4x）\n- **CP-SAT 没有公开 WASM benchmark**，但同类 Z3 报告 native 的 20-50% 性能\n- 多线程：浏览器需 SharedArrayBuffer + COOP/COEP 头；服务端 wasi-threads 还在 proposal\n\n## 5. 工具链 + Runtime\n\n- **Emscripten**：5.0.x（2026 dev），LLVM Wasm 后端默认，POSIX 仿真完整，编 OR-Tools 的现实选择\n- **Wasmtime**：WASI Preview 2 / Component Model 标杆，~3ms 冷启动 / 15MB 内存\n- **Wasmer**：~2ms / 12MB，AOT+JIT，pip 安装最简单\n- **WasmEdge**：1.5ms / 8MB，边缘+AI 硬件加速最强（但对你项目没用）\n\n## 6. 暂无的能力\n\n- WebAssembly Component Model **没有 SAT/CP solver 组件**（也没人在做）\n- WebGPU + 求解：2025-2026 GPU 求解大势是 NVIDIA cuOpt（CUDA，PDLP/PDHG），**没有 WebGPU LP/MIP solver 项目**\n- 浏览器内跑 placement solver 的 demo：**搜不到**，Z3/MiniSat demo 都是玩具规模\n\n## 对我们项目可行性判断\n\n**结论：12 月观察，不投入 PoC。**\n\n理由按重要性：\n\n1. **168h 长跑场景与 WASM 强项不匹配**。WASM 的卖点是冷启动快、跨平台分发、安全沙箱——你需要的是稳定多线程长跑，恰好是 WASM 当前最弱的两块（线程标准化没落地，沙箱内长跑工具链不成熟）\n2. **CP-SAT WASM build 第三方 solver 全砍**。你的项目主力就是 CP-SAT，砍掉的是辅助路径，但 OR-Tools 官方零人力投入，长期维护风险高\n3. **多核性能损失不可接受**。你 S6 阶段 8-profile worker matrix 重度依赖 native 多线程 CP-SAT，WASM 走 SharedArrayBuffer 在浏览器内能跑但服务端 wasi-threads 还是 proposal，多核性能保守估计 native 的 50-70%，168h 场景这是几十小时差距\n4. **跨平台部署的真实需求弱**。Linux 容器有现成 Docker，比 WASM 成熟太多；浏览器跑 placement solver 是玩具用途（你的实例规模 70x70 + 266 facility 不是\"用户点一下\"场景）；边缘设备没有用例\n5. **AI sidecar 路线（lane C）反而更可能用到 WASM**——如果将来想把 AI 推理客户端化做交互式 demo，那时候再看\n\n**触发重新评估的信号**：(a) wasi-threads 进入 WASI 1.0；(b) OR-Tools 官方发布 WASM release artifact；(c) 出现 CaDiCaL 或 Kissat 的官方 WASM 端口并跑过 SAT Competition 基准\n\n短期建议：保持现有 native 部署，把跨平台诉求放到 Docker/Linux ARM64 这条已经成熟的路上。WASM 这条线 2026 年底再看一次。\n\nSources:\n- [OR-Tools Issue #4443 - WASM compile feasibility](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4443)\n- [OR-Tools Issue #1670 - browser-friendly emscripten](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1670)\n- [OR-Tools discuss - Compiling to WebAssembly](https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/ESK9oknRrK8)\n- [WASI 0.3 native async](https://byteiota.com/wasi-0-3-native-async-webassembly-gets-concurrent-i-o/)\n- [Hypercharge Through Components - WASI 0.3](https://medium.com/wasm-radar/hypercharge-through-components-why-wasi-0-3-and-composable-concurrency-are-a-game-changer-0852e673830a)\n- [WASI 1.0 timeline - The New Stack](https://thenewstack.io/wasi-1-0-you-wont-know-when-webassembly-is-everywhere-in-2026/)\n- [wasi-threads proposal](https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-threads)\n- [WebAssembly Runtime Benchmarks 2026](https://wasmruntime.com/en/benchmarks)\n- [Wasmtime vs Wasmer vs WasmEdge 2026](https://reintech.io/blog/wasmtime-vs-wasmer-vs-wasmedge-wasm-runtime-comparison-2026)\n- [State of WebAssembly 2025-2026](https://platform.uno/blog/the-state-of-webassembly-2025-2026/)\n- [CaDiCaL/Kissat SAT Competition 2025 paper](https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2025-solvers.pdf)\n- [Kissat GitHub](https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat)\n- [z3.wasm builds](https://github.com/cpitclaudel/z3.wasm)\n- [z3-solver npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/z3-solver)\n- [MiniSat WASM demo](https://jgalenson.github.io/research.js/demos/minisat.html)\n- [minisat-wasm GitHub](https://github.com/glnc/minisat-wasm)\n- [Rust+Wasm 8-10x perf 2025 benchmarks](https://byteiota.com/rust-webassembly-performance-8-10x-faster-2025-benchmarks/)\n- [Boosting WASM with SIMD and threads - InfoQ](https://www.infoq.com/articles/webassembly-simd-multithreading-performance-gains/)\n- [Analyzing Performance of WebAssembly vs Native (USENIX ATC '19)](https://www.usenix.org/system/files/atc19-jangda.pdf)\n- [Emscripten docs](https://emscripten.org/docs/compiling/WebAssembly.html)\n- [NVIDIA cuOpt - GPU LP/MIP](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuopt)\n- [HiGHS + cuOpt collaboration](https://blogs.ed.ac.uk/mathematics/2025/03/18/highs-and-nvidia-cuopt-driving-open-source-innovation-in-optimization/)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1313,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3358,"cache_read_input_tokens":32979,"output_tokens":3258,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3358},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1313,"output_tokens":3258,"cache_read_input_tokens":32979,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3358,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxpL8MLWZjapYYn6fBW","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"8654cb58-f4ff-4bc3-b968-a93424baafd9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:03:20.037Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
